{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoEngine\/documentation\/GnustoEngine\/Fuse\/init(initialTurns:repeats:action:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoEngine\/documentation\/GnustoEngine\/Fuse\/action","doc:\/\/GnustoEngine\/documentation\/GnustoEngine\/Fuse\/initialTurns","doc:\/\/GnustoEngine\/documentation\/GnustoEngine\/Fuse\/repeats"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustoengine\/fuse"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Fuse"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/GnustoEngine\/documentation\/GnustoEngine\/GnustoAutoWiringPlugin"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Fuses are classic ZIL features used to implement delayed actions or events. They can be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simple timers (like a bomb fuse) or complex context-aware events (like enemy recovery","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with specific location and enemy data). When activated, fuses can optionally store custom","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state data that persists until the event triggers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You create "},{"code":"Fuse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instances and register them with the "},{"code":"GameBlueprint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when setting up your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game. To start a timed event, you would then use a game command or side effect to activate"},{"type":"text","tex